      "content": "interesting. so when i'm in clinical rotations, is it basically standard practice to account for those differences when deciding on dosages? like, are there specific biological reasons why black patients might need more opioids, or is it more about how their bodies process the medication differently? i just want to make sure i understand the underlying mechanism so i don't make assumptions.",
